From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Fedora: check the follow-up sandbox and retain stock SELinux labels

Build the exact GBM/worker policy correction and run the four source/config
contracts natively. The tablet's signed original Fedora policy already assigns
bin_t and chrome_sandbox_exec_t to the packaged paths. Keep restorecon over
the entire browser directory; remove redundant, incorrect unversioned local
semanage rules and their additional Python dependency chain.

Applies after 0003-fedora156-arm-vaapi-test-package.patch, based on Fedora
e402dd33400be892fc94d8c1f2fab15c9dc81c9b. Full native RPM and installed SELinux,
sandbox and GL/video verification remain separate gates.

--- a/chromium.spec
+++ b/chromium.spec
@@ -283,7 +283,7 @@
 
 Name:	chromium
 Version: 156.0.8078.47
-Release: 1.1.uke2%{?dist}
+Release: 1.1.uke3%{?dist}
 Summary: A WebKit (Blink) powered web browser that Google doesn't want you to use
 Url: http://www.chromium.org/Home
 License: BSD-3-Clause AND LGPL-2.1-or-later AND Apache-2.0 AND IJG AND MIT AND GPL-2.0-or-later AND ISC AND OpenSSL AND (MPL-1.1 OR GPL-2.0-only OR LGPL-2.0-only)
@@ -558,6 +558,7 @@
 # Linux ARM Mesa sandbox candidate; no persistent runtime feature bypass.
 Patch600: 0001-chromium156-linux-arm-mesa-sandbox.patch
 Patch601: 0002-chromium156-linux-arm-iris-sandbox.patch
+Patch602: 0004-chromium156-mesa-gbm-worker-sandbox.patch
 
 # Upstream patches
 
@@ -604,8 +605,14 @@
 Source17: https://registry.npmjs.org/@esbuild/linux-arm64/-/linux-arm64-%{esbuild_version}.tgz
 %endif
 
+Source600: chromium-arm-sandbox-contract.sh
+Source601: chromium-iris-sandbox-contract.sh
+Source602: chromium-gbm-scheduling-contract.sh
+Source603: chromium-default-flags-contract.sh
+
 BuildRequires: golang
 BuildRequires: clang
+BuildRequires: gcc-c++
 BuildRequires: clang-tools-extra
 BuildRequires: llvm
 BuildRequires: lld
@@ -1059,7 +1066,6 @@
 
 %if %{undefined flatpak}
 # For selinux scriptlet
-Requires(post): /usr/sbin/semanage
 Requires(post): /usr/sbin/restorecon
 %endif
 
@@ -1291,6 +1297,7 @@
 
 %patch -P600 -p1 -b .linux-arm-mesa-sandbox
 %patch -P601 -p1 -b .linux-arm-iris-sandbox
+%patch -P602 -p1 -b .mesa-gbm-worker-sandbox
 
 # Upstream patches
 
@@ -1745,6 +1752,12 @@
 %build_target %{chromebuilddir} chrome_management_service
 %endif
 
+%check
+CXX=g++ bash %{SOURCE600} content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
+CXX=g++ bash %{SOURCE601} content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
+CXX=g++ bash %{SOURCE602} content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc sandbox/policy/linux/bpf_gpu_policy_linux.cc
+bash %{SOURCE603} %{SOURCE2}
+
 %install
 rm -rf %{buildroot}
 
@@ -1861,13 +1874,9 @@
 
 %if %{undefined flatpak}
 %post
-# Set SELinux labels - semanage itself will adjust the lib directory naming
-# But only do it when selinux is enabled, otherwise, it gets noisy.
+# Fedora policy already labels this directory and its privileged helper.
 if selinuxenabled; then
-	semanage fcontext -a -t bin_t /usr/lib/chromium-browser &>/dev/null || :
-	semanage fcontext -a -t bin_t /usr/lib/chromium-browser/chromium-browser.sh &>/dev/null || :
-	semanage fcontext -a -t chrome_sandbox_exec_t /usr/lib/chrome-sandbox &>/dev/null || :
-	restorecon -R -v %{chromium_path}/chromium-browser &>/dev/null || :
+	restorecon -R -v %{chromium_path} &>/dev/null || :
 fi
 %endif
 
@@ -1996,6 +2005,11 @@
 %endif
 
 %changelog
+* Mon Oct 26 2026 MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com> - 156.0.8078.47-1.1.uke3
+- Admit the exact Mesa GBM module read and refuse optional ARM64 batch hints.
+- Keep graphics feature defaults and enable early, fatal ARM64 GPU sandboxing.
+- Verify source/config contracts and retain Fedora SELinux labels without local rules.
+
 * Wed Oct 21 2026 Than Ngo <than@redhat.com> - 156.0.8078.47-1
 - Update to 156.0.8078.47, include 353 security fixes
   * CVE-2026-112992: Memory corruption in Canvas
